# vendor/ is COMMITTED on purpose. There is no composer install on the target
# host: the release archive carries the tree itself, and release/build-update.php
# builds that archive from a GIT DIFF, so an untracked package cannot ship.
#
# This line used to read "/vendor", and the tree was force-added past it. That
# silently dropped every package Composer added afterwards, because `git add -A`
# and `git add -u` both skip ignored paths - 1037 files by the time TODO 35.1
# measured it. Ignoring nothing here is what makes the ordinary commit flow, the
# builder's dirty-tree check and `git status --porcelain vendor/` all work.
#
# The IDE cache is the one thing under vendor/ that Composer did not put there.
/vendor/_laravel_ide/
# Update archives built by release/build-update.php
/release/dist
